    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** offense is anchored today by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, whose 81.59 score makes him our premier start against Kade Anderson. The combination of his base profile and the favorable platoon advantage against a southpaw pushes his ceiling significantly higher than the rest of the cohort. **Gunnar Henderson** (78.37) and **Kyle Tucker** (75.96) follow close behind; **Gunnar Henderson** is poised for a high-output day bolstered by a generous 10% park factor, while **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a strong matchup against Montero. At catcher, **Drake Baldwin** (71.33) is a prioritized start, as his leadoff spot against the struggling Ryan Feltner (5.07 xERA) provides maximum volume in what projects to be an efficient outing.\n\nTactical optimization favored **Nasim Nunez** and **Dominic Smith** despite their marginal efficiency scores, largely due to their specific skill sets. **Nasim Nunez** offers critical stolen base potential against Sandy Alcantara, helping us attack the scarcity in that category, while **Dominic Smith** remains in the lineup to leverage the platoon advantage against Feltner. The most difficult bench decision involved **Tommy White**, who produced a 54.63 score. While **Tommy White** benefits from a significant 10% park boost, the optimizer ultimately favored the higher positional floor of our active starters. We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Liam Hicks**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**; any shifts in batting order, particularly for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** at the #3 spot or **Nasim Nunez** at the #9 spot, could necessitate late-day roster adjustments. **Luis Robert Jr.** represents a notable risk today; while his 62.99 score is solid, he faces an \"Elite Hold\" pitcher, which diminishes his stolen base probability by 4%.",
